without SA_RESTART:
  child: ISIG is on, VINTR is 3 (Ctrl-C), blocking in read
  parent: typing Ctrl-C (byte 0x03) on the master side
  child: read returned -1, errno 4 (Interrupted system call), handler ran: yes
  child exit status 0 -> acceptance test PASS
with SA_RESTART:
  child: ISIG is on, VINTR is 3 (Ctrl-C), blocking in read
  parent: typing Ctrl-C (byte 0x03) on the master side
  parent: typing "ok" and Enter, so a restarted read can finish
  child: read returned 3, errno 0 (none), handler ran: yes
  child exit status 1 -> the read was restarted, as SA_RESTART asks
U1 signal test (without SA_RESTART): PASS
